# spread: the frames a clip's median of dropped frames may exceed the most
# Linux dropped in one play of that clip, on the Lenovo, for each browser,
# which `judge.py video` reads as SPREAD (tests/native/gpuvideo.sh browsers).
# A line is `BROWSER FRAMES`.
#
# Both browsers decode the clips in software but for Firefox's H.264, so
# their drops measure processor time and frame timing, and they vary from
# play to play on either system. The judge has three counted plays a side,
# and the median of one side's three exceeds the most of the other's in 4 of
# the 20 orders of six untied counts, so with no spread a system that drops
# as Linux does fails one clip in five.
#
# FRAMES is the widest range of one clip's three counted plays in that
# browser's run of linux.tar.gz, the reference beside this file: Chromium's
# AV1 720p dropped 24, 24 and 3, Firefox's AV1 1080p 0, 22 and 2. A new
# reference takes its own widest range here.
chromium 21
firefox 22
